    {
      "id": "source-8",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T10:50:00Z",
      "note": "The attacker EOA created two contracts and then sent six transactions to the exploit contract; the anchor is the first of them and its trace is a bare successful listToken through the bridge proxy, which is the defect executing with no value moving yet. The remaining five carry the withdrawTokens legs, so the loss is measured across all six. The proxy is an OwnedUpgradeabilityProxy that does not use the EIP-1967 slot; it emitted exactly five Upgraded events between its creation block 18391304 and the exploit, the last at block 19720066 installing 0x354cca2f55dde182d36fe34d673430e226a3cb8c, and the anchor trace shows the proxy delegate-calling that implementation, which fixes both the artifact and the 12.2-hour age. Its creator 0xfe6fb9ded2651fd325512657d34911d2fb5d646b is not the attacker. The v1 record’s deployment block was the last upgrade block rather than the proxy creation block; that is corrected here."
    }
  ],
